{# Carried by every screen that writes to a class's COPY of library content.

   The copy and the model are edited through forms that look identical on purpose (see
   App\Form\SeanceInstanceType), so this banner is the only thing that says which of the two the
   teacher is about to change. It states three things, in this order, because that is the order the
   questions arise in: where you are, what it will not do, and what it will do.

   `cohortLabel` names the class; `templateTitle` is the library séquence this copy came from, or
   null when the copy has no model - written straight for this class, or its model deleted since. #}
<div class="cm-instance-banner">
    <span class="cm-instance-banner__icon" aria-hidden="true">✎</span>
    <div class="cm-instance-banner__body">
        <p class="cm-instance-banner__title">{{ 'instanceEditBannerTitle'|trans({'%class%': cohortLabel}) }}</p>
        <p class="cm-instance-banner__text">
            {% if templateTitle %}
                {{ 'instanceEditBannerModelText'|trans({'%template%': templateTitle}) }}
            {% else %}
                {{ 'instanceEditBannerNoModelText'|trans }}
            {% endif %}
        </p>
        <p class="cm-instance-banner__text">{{ 'instanceEditBannerImpactText'|trans({'%class%': cohortLabel}) }}</p>
    </div>
</div>
